/*
 * BUGBUSTER LOCAL OVERRIDE of lib/debugprobe/src/probe.pio.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: upstream's probe_sm_init() sets the SWCLK/SWDIO pin
 * directions with a single pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs() based at
 * PROBE_PIN_OFFSET, which only works when the two pins are adjacent. The
 * BugBuster HAT routes SWCLK to GPIO18 and SWDIO to GPIO16, so
 * src/board_bugbuster_hat_config.h defines the two pins individually and does
 * NOT define PROBE_PIN_OFFSET -- upstream's version therefore fails to compile
 * with "'PROBE_PIN_OFFSET' undeclared".
 *
 * This lives in the superproject rather than in the debugprobe submodule on
 * purpose. The same fix was previously made inside the submodule, was never
 * pushed to the fork, and was silently lost -- CI only caught it months later,
 * on the first release that rebuilt the RP2040. src/probe_config.h is already
 * overridden the same way (it selects the board header via BB_HAT_FIRMWARE),
 * so this matches the established pattern.
 *
 * CMakeLists.txt generates the PIO header from THIS file, not the submodule's.
 * When bumping the debugprobe submodule, re-diff against
 * lib/debugprobe/src/probe.pio and re-apply the marked override below.
 *
 * Base: debugprobe v2.3.0 (submodule commit 780b827).
 */

